&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Textio (Lavalier)&lt;/strong&gt; | San Francisco, CA (hybrid, 2–3 days/week in office)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation:&lt;/strong&gt; $125,000–$150,000 base | $250,000–$300,000 OTE (50/50 split)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About Lavalier&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lavalier is Textio&#39;s interview intelligence platform, built on a simple belief: hiring faster only matters if you&#39;re also hiring the right people. Most tools in this space stop at transcription — efficiency without quality. Lavalier is different. We coach interviewers in the moment, when it actually changes outcomes, rather than handing them a transcript after the fact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The market signal is clear: talent leaders want this. Companies like Bloomberg, Cisco, Johnson &amp;amp; Johnson, Samsung, and Spotify already trust Textio. Now we&#39;re looking for the person who will drive awareness of Lavalier, land our foundational customers, and build the sales motion from the ground up.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About the role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a true founding Enterprise AE role. You&#39;ll run your book like it&#39;s your own business — sourcing your own pipeline, executing deals end to end, and shaping how we go to market. You&#39;ll work directly with our CEO and VP of Marketing, and your fingerprints will be on everything from messaging to pricing conversations to product feedback.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Generate your own pipeline.&lt;/strong&gt; Build and execute an outbound plan focused on one-to-one outreach and account targeting — mid- and lower-funnel work, not mass email cadences.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Execute deals end to end.&lt;/strong&gt; Develop relationships across the full buying team, share content that moves each stakeholder, and coordinate internally with our operations team on technical, security, and procurement questions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Project manage every deal.&lt;/strong&gt; Know every deadline, know who owns what, and follow up proactively (and respectfully) when things stall — whether that&#39;s a buyer going quiet or an NDA sitting with a contracts team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partner closely with marketing.&lt;/strong&gt; Stay aligned on who owns what, push for the content and one-pagers you need, and avoid redundant or competing motions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Know the product.&lt;/strong&gt; Demo Lavalier and Textio&#39;s recruiting and feedback products effectively, and match the right product to where a company is in its lifecycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Provide product feedback.&lt;/strong&gt; Bring structured, useful product feedback back to the team. As a founding AE, you&#39;re the voice of the market inside the company.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What we&#39;re looking for&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Full-cycle B2B sales experience with a track record of hitting quota, ideally in HR tech, recruiting tech, or selling to talent acquisition and HR leaders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proven outbound motion — you&#39;ve succeeded in environments where you sourced most of your own pipeline, not one where inbound did the work for you&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience navigating multi-stakeholder deals: building champions, managing procurement and security reviews, and keeping momentum through long cycles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort with ambiguity and early-stage pace&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong project management instincts and proactive communication, internally and externally&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Based in San Francisco and able to be in office 2–3 days per week&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus points&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Former recruiter or talent acquisition background — you&#39;ve lived the problem we solve&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience selling into or alongside ATS ecosystems (Workday, Greenhouse, Ashby, iCIMS)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Founding or first-AE experience at an early-stage company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Why this role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The need is real and the timing is right. Talent leaders are already convinced they should be recording and transcribing interviews — the next step is showing them that transcription alone doesn&#39;t improve hiring quality. You&#39;ll be the one making that case, with a differentiated product, strong integrations across the most common ATSs, and direct access to leadership. Few sales roles offer this much ownership over the outcome.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Textio is an equal opportunity employer. We celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
